# shellcheck shell=bash
# Invocation behind the Spanish V100 control of the multilingual wave
# (audit finding NEW-05, docs/next_control.md), whose comparison with the
# four arms is output/evaluation/fleurs_es419_v100_control.json: Whisper
# Large v3 on the whole es_419 FLEURS test split, scored raw, at the fourth
# arm's code (6f9bf56) on a V100, the card family the third arm decoded
# Spanish on.
#
# Two jobs of task 2 (es_419, spanish), account <project-b>, partition
# short, QoS standard, four cores, 32 GB and one gpu:v100, submitted on
# 2026-10-17 and run on 2026-10-19 from the clone
# ~/paper_speech_transcription_ctl_es419 at 6f9bf56 with a clean tree, as
# both environment records and both summaries' run_metadata say:
#   9124739_2  pf_es419_v100   WER_ML_LIMIT=5, 30 min limit   Tesla V100-PCIE-32GB  htc-g003
#   9124863_2  ctl_es419_v100  the full split, 2 h limit      Tesla V100-PCIE-32GB  htc-g004
# The pre-flight wrote into controls/es_419_v100_6f9bf56_preflight. The
# commands of docs/next_control.md had the full split wait for the
# pre-flight and allowed it 12 h; it was released before the pre-flight ran
# and given 2 h, and it took 52 min. Both were submitted with the values
# below exported by hand; this file, written afterwards, records them.
#
# WER_ML_MODEL is the script's default at 6f9bf56, written out so that a
# later change of the default cannot change what this record reproduces;
# WER_ML_CONDITIONS keeps the raw hypothesis alone, the decode under test.
# WER_ML_LIMIT is set empty, which the script reads as the whole split.
# The module the script runs, evaluation/benchmark_wer.py, has changed
# since 6f9bf56 (f0ac4e3 added --device and --dtype), so a reproduction
# meant to match runs from a checkout of 6f9bf56, with this file copied
# into its hpc/runs/ from a current clone. At 6f9bf56 the environment
# record and the summary's run_metadata ask git about tracked files only,
# so the untracked copy does not mark the run as modified.
#
# Reproduce (from the root of a checkout of 6f9bf56 on ARC). The command
# stops at "|| exit 1" when the record is missing. Without it, bash carries
# on past a "." that cannot find its file, and sbatch submits the script
# with its own defaults, which write into the evaluation directory itself.
#   ( set -a; . hpc/runs/fleurs_es419_v100.env || exit 1; set +a
#     sbatch --clusters=htc --partition=short --account='<your-project>' --qos=standard \
#       --array=2 --ntasks=1 --cpus-per-task=4 --mem=32G --time=02:00:00 \
#       --gres=gpu:v100:1 --job-name=ctl_es419_v100 \
#       hpc/submit_benchmark_wer_multilingual.sh )
#
# A reproduction writes to its own directory under repro/, so it cannot
# overwrite the ARC copy of the original run it is to be compared with, and
# the script refuses to write a task's summary over an existing one unless
# OVERWRITE=1.
# original: WER_ML_OUTPUT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/controls/es_419_v100_6f9bf56"
WER_ML_MODEL=openai/whisper-large-v3
WER_ML_CONDITIONS=raw
WER_ML_LIMIT=
WER_ML_OUTPUT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/repro/fleurs_es419_v100"
